135-16020-0031 V:0.4604 A:0.4063 D:0.4859 FLUNG THE OTHER OVER THE OUTER WALL CROSSED THE ABYSS AT ONE BOUND CLUNG TO THE COPING OF THE WALL GOT ASTRIDE OF IT LET THEMSELVES SLIP ONE AFTER THE OTHER ALONG THE ROPE UPON A LITTLE ROOF WHICH TOUCHES THE BATH HOUSE THREE
135-16020-0032 V:0.3829 A:0.3460 D:0.4489 QUARTERS OF AN HOUR HAD NOT ELAPSED SINCE THEY HAD RISEN IN BED IN THE DARK NAIL IN HAND AND THEIR PROJECT IN THEIR HEADS
135-16020-0033 V:0.4808 A:0.3732 D:0.4756 A FEW MOMENTS LATER THEY HAD JOINED BABET AND MONTPARNASSE WHO WERE PROWLING ABOUT THE NEIGHBORHOOD
135-16020-0034 V:0.5203 A:0.3893 D:0.4792 AND A BIT OF IT REMAINED ATTACHED TO THE CHIMNEY ON THE ROOF
135-16020-0035 V:0.2821 A:0.3814 D:0.5047 THEY HAD SUSTAINED NO OTHER DAMAGE HOWEVER THAN THAT OF SCRATCHING NEARLY ALL THE SKIN OFF THEIR HANDS
135-16020-0037 V:0.5159 A:0.4262 D:0.5123 THIS WAS BRUJON
135-16020-0038 V:0.4709 A:0.3286 D:0.4421 THENARDIER RECOGNIZED HIM AND UNDERSTOOD
135-16020-0039 V:0.3116 A:0.3496 D:0.4705 THIS WAS ENOUGH
135-16020-0040 V:0.2903 A:0.3364 D:0.4605 THENARDIER RATED AS A BURGLAR WITH ARMED FORCE WAS KEPT IN SIGHT
135-16020-0041 V:0.3648 A:0.3868 D:0.5076 THE SENTRY WHO WAS RELIEVED EVERY TWO HOURS MARCHED UP AND DOWN IN FRONT OF HIS CAGE WITH LOADED MUSKET
135-16020-0042 V:0.4041 A:0.3797 D:0.5012 THE PRISONER HAD ON HIS FEET FETTERS WEIGHING FIFTY POUNDS
135-16020-0043 V:0.4028 A:0.3862 D:0.5000 EVERY DAY AT FOUR OCLOCK IN THE AFTERNOON A JAILER ESCORTED BY TWO DOGS THIS WAS STILL IN VOGUE AT THAT TIME ENTERED HIS CAGE DEPOSITED BESIDE HIS BED A LOAF OF BLACK BREAD
135-16020-0044 V:0.4546 A:0.4029 D:0.5067 THENARDIER HAD OBTAINED PERMISSION TO KEEP A SORT OF IRON BOLT WHICH HE USED TO SPIKE HIS BREAD INTO A CRACK IN THE WALL IN ORDER TO PRESERVE IT FROM THE RATS AS HE SAID
135-16020-0045 V:0.2635 A:0.3738 D:0.4938 NO OBJECTION HAD BEEN MADE TO THIS SPIKE
135-16020-0046 V:0.4399 A:0.4011 D:0.4970 STILL IT WAS REMEMBERED AFTERWARDS THAT ONE OF THE JAILERS HAD SAID IT WOULD BE BETTER TO LET HIM HAVE ONLY A WOODEN SPIKE
135-16020-0047 V:0.3676 A:0.3402 D:0.4603 AT TWO OCLOCK IN THE MORNING THE SENTINEL WHO WAS AN OLD SOLDIER
135-16041-0000 V:0.3377 A:0.4542 D:0.5422 THESE MELANCHOLY OPENINGS WHICH TAKE PLACE IN THE GLOOM BEFORE DESPAIR ARE TEMPTING MARIUS THRUST ASIDE THE BAR WHICH HAD SO OFTEN ALLOWED HIM TO PASS EMERGED FROM THE GARDEN AND SAID I WILL GO
135-16041-0001 V:0.4304 A:0.5651 D:0.6430 MAD WITH GRIEF NO LONGER CONSCIOUS OF ANYTHING FIXED OR SOLID IN HIS BRAIN INCAPABLE OF ACCEPTING ANYTHING THENCEFORTH OF FATE AFTER THOSE TWO MONTHS PASSED IN THE INTOXICATION OF YOUTH AND LOVE OVERWHELMED AT ONCE BY ALL THE REVERIES OF DESPAIR HE HAD BUT ONE DESIRE REMAINING TO MAKE A SPEEDY END OF ALL
135-16041-0002 V:0.4852 A:0.4250 D:0.5227 HE SET OUT AT RAPID PACE
135-16041-0003 V:0.4837 A:0.5342 D:0.6256 HE FOUND HIMSELF MOST OPPORTUNELY ARMED
135-16041-0004 V:0.4707 A:0.4388 D:0.5224 BY THE BOULEVARD TRAVERSED THE ESPLANADE AND THE BRIDGE OF THE INVALIDES AND REACHED THE RUE DE RIVOLI
135-16041-0005 V:0.5015 A:0.5010 D:0.5802 THE SHOPS WERE OPEN THERE WOMEN WERE MAKING THEIR PURCHASES IN THE STALLS PEOPLE WERE EATING ICES IN THE CAFE LAITER AND NIBBLING SMALL CAKES AT THE ENGLISH PASTRY COOKS SHOP
135-16041-0006 V:0.4993 A:0.4653 D:0.5416 AND AT THE SAME TIME THE CROWD INCREASED IN DENSITY
135-16041-0007 V:0.4793 A:0.4690 D:0.5613 FOR THE PASSERS BY NOW AMOUNTED TO A CROWD
135-16041-0008 V:0.4203 A:0.4675 D:0.5556 NO ONE COULD BE SEEN TO SPEAK IN THIS THRONG AND YET THERE AROSE FROM IT A DULL DEEP MURMUR
135-16041-0009 V:0.4308 A:0.4487 D:0.5215 NEAR THE FOUNTAIN OF THE ARBRE SEC THERE WERE ASSEMBLAGES MOTIONLESS AND GLOOMY GROUPS WHICH WERE TO THOSE WHO WENT AND CAME AS STONES IN THE MIDST OF RUNNING WATER
135-16041-0011 V:0.4007 A:0.5686 D:0.6407 THERE WERE HARDLY ANY BLACK COATS OR ROUND HATS NOW BUT SMOCK FROCKS BLOUSES CAPS AND BRISTLING AND CADAVEROUS HEADS
135-16041-0012 V:0.4601 A:0.4943 D:0.5750 THIS MULTITUDE UNDULATED CONFUSEDLY IN THE NOCTURNAL GLOOM
135-16041-0013 V:0.5930 A:0.4469 D:0.5641 ITS WHISPERINGS HAD THE HOARSE ACCENT OF A VIBRATION
135-16041-0014 V:0.3210 A:0.4544 D:0.5585 ALTHOUGH NOT ONE OF THEM WAS WALKING A DULL TRAMPLING WAS AUDIBLE IN THE MIRE
135-16041-0015 V:0.4757 A:0.4144 D:0.5109 BEYOND THIS DENSE PORTION OF THE THRONG IN THE RUE DU ROULE IN THE RUE DES PROUVAIRES
135-16041-0016 V:0.4460 A:0.4389 D:0.5262 ONLY THE SOLITARY AND DIMINISHING ROWS OF LANTERNS COULD BE SEEN VANISHING INTO THE STREET IN THE DISTANCE
135-16041-0017 V:0.4945 A:0.5182 D:0.5812 THE LANTERNS OF THAT DATE RESEMBLED LARGE RED STARS HANGING TO ROPES AND SHED UPON THE PAVEMENT A SHADOW WHICH HAD THE FORM OF A HUGE SPIDER
135-16041-0018 V:0.2092 A:0.3457 D:0.4703 THESE STREETS WERE NOT DESERTED
135-16041-0019 V:0.4605 A:0.4983 D:0.5782 THERE COULD BE DESCRIED PILES OF GUNS MOVING BAYONETS AND TROOPS BIVOUACKING
135-16041-0020 V:0.4409 A:0.4306 D:0.5250 NO CURIOUS OBSERVER PASSED THAT LIMIT
135-16041-0021 V:0.3850 A:0.4286 D:0.5077 THERE CIRCULATION CEASED
135-16041-0022 V:0.3812 A:0.4044 D:0.5276 THERE THE RABBLE ENDED AND THE ARMY BEGAN
135-16041-0023 V:0.4540 A:0.3286 D:0.4584 MARIUS WILLED WITH THE WILL OF A MAN WHO HOPES NO MORE
135-16041-0024 V:0.3308 A:0.3555 D:0.4475 HE HAD BEEN SUMMONED HE MUST GO
135-16041-0025 V:0.3415 A:0.4453 D:0.5471 HE FOUND A MEANS TO TRAVERSE THE THRONG HE SHUNNED THE PATROLS HE AVOIDED THE SENTINELS
135-16041-0026 V:0.5432 A:0.5167 D:0.5658 HE MADE A CIRCUIT REACHED THE RUE DE BETHISY
135-16041-0027 V:0.3090 A:0.3910 D:0.4651 THERE WERE NO LONGER ANY LANTERNS
135-16041-0028 V:0.4106 A:0.4392 D:0.5155 AFTER HAVING PASSED THE ZONE OF THE CROWD HE HAD PASSED THE LIMITS OF THE TROOPS HE FOUND HIMSELF IN SOMETHING STARTLING
135-16041-0029 V:0.3449 A:0.4971 D:0.5830 THERE WAS NO LONGER A PASSER BY NO LONGER A SOLDIER NO LONGER A LIGHT THERE WAS NO ONE SOLITUDE SILENCE NIGHT
135-16041-0030 V:0.2657 A:0.2897 D:0.3974 ENTERING A STREET WAS LIKE ENTERING A CELLAR
135-16041-0031 V:0.4522 A:0.3333 D:0.4532 HE CONTINUED TO ADVANCE
135-16041-0032 V:0.3749 A:0.3459 D:0.4282 HE TOOK A FEW STEPS
135-16041-0033 V:0.3840 A:0.4154 D:0.4779 SOME ONE PASSED CLOSE TO HIM AT A RUN
135-16041-0034 V:0.3614 A:0.5275 D:0.5308 WAS IT A MAN
135-16041-0035 V:0.3631 A:0.4724 D:0.5386 OR A WOMAN
135-16041-0036 V:0.3022 A:0.4085 D:0.4642 WERE THERE MANY OF THEM
135-16041-0037 V:0.2882 A:0.3725 D:0.4509 HE COULD NOT HAVE TOLD
135-16041-0038 V:0.4006 A:0.2521 D:0.3555 IT HAD PASSED AND VANISHED
135-16041-0039 V:0.4442 A:0.4817 D:0.5531 PROCEEDING FROM CIRCUIT TO CIRCUIT HE REACHED A LANE WHICH HE JUDGED TO BE THE RUE DE LA POTERIE NEAR THE MIDDLE OF THIS STREET
135-16041-0040 V:0.3670 A:0.4126 D:0.4937 IT WAS AN OVERTURNED WAGON HIS FOOT RECOGNIZED POOLS OF WATER GULLIES AND PAVING STONES SCATTERED AND PILED UP
135-16041-0041 V:0.4259 A:0.4009 D:0.5004 HE CLIMBED OVER THE STONES AND FOUND HIMSELF ON THE OTHER SIDE OF THE BARRIER
135-16041-0042 V:0.4695 A:0.3489 D:0.4648 HE WALKED VERY NEAR THE STREET POSTS AND GUIDED HIMSELF ALONG THE WALLS OF THE HOUSES
135-16041-0043 V:0.3224 A:0.4067 D:0.4864 A LITTLE BEYOND THE BARRICADE IT SEEMED TO HIM
135-16041-0044 V:0.2875 A:0.3218 D:0.4467 MARIUS LEFT THE HORSES BEHIND HIM
135-16041-0045 V:0.3914 A:0.4586 D:0.5318 AS HE WAS APPROACHING A STREET WHICH SEEMED TO HIM TO BE THE RUE DU CONTRAT SOCIAL A SHOT COMING NO ONE KNOWS WHENCE AND TRAVERSING THE DARKNESS AT RANDOM WHISTLED CLOSE BY HIM
135-16041-0046 V:0.3755 A:0.4007 D:0.5158 THE WHOLE OF THIS ITINERARY
135-16041-0047 V:0.5007 A:0.3718 D:0.4780 WHICH IS LIKE A CITY WITHIN A CITY HOLLOWED OUT IN THE CENTRE OF PARIS
135-16041-0048 V:0.3174 A:0.4512 D:0.5356 THERE THE GLANCE FELL INTO AN ABYSS
135-16041-0049 V:0.6054 A:0.5528 D:0.6190 THANKS TO THE BROKEN LANTERNS THANKS TO THE CLOSED WINDOWS THERE ALL RADIANCE ALL LIFE ALL SOUND ALL MOVEMENT CEASED
135-16041-0050 V:0.3540 A:0.4480 D:0.5545 THE INVISIBLE POLICE OF THE INSURRECTION WERE ON THE WATCH EVERYWHERE AND MAINTAINED ORDER THAT IS TO SAY NIGHT
135-16041-0052 V:0.3365 A:0.5292 D:0.5955 AT DUSK EVERY WINDOW WHERE A CANDLE WAS BURNING RECEIVED A SHOT
135-16041-0053 V:0.1998 A:0.4941 D:0.5844 THE LIGHT WAS EXTINGUISHED SOMETIMES THE INHABITANT WAS KILLED
135-16041-0054 V:0.2424 A:0.3631 D:0.4594 HENCE NOTHING WAS STIRRING
135-16041-0055 V:0.1952 A:0.5081 D:0.5936 THERE WAS NOTHING BUT FRIGHT MOURNING STUPOR IN THE HOUSES AND IN THE STREETS A SORT OF SACRED HORROR
135-16041-0056 V:0.4108 A:0.4748 D:0.5496 NOT EVEN THE LONG ROWS OF WINDOWS AND STORES THE INDENTATIONS OF THE CHIMNEYS AND THE ROOFS AND THE VAGUE REFLECTIONS WHICH ARE CAST BACK BY THE WET AND MUDDY PAVEMENTS WERE VISIBLE
135-16041-0057 V:0.4465 A:0.4437 D:0.5101 AN EYE CAST UPWARD AT THAT MASS OF SHADOWS MIGHT PERHAPS HAVE CAUGHT A GLIMPSE HERE AND THERE AT INTERVALS OF INDISTINCT GLEAMS WHICH BROUGHT OUT BROKEN AND ECCENTRIC LINES AND PROFILES OF SINGULAR BUILDINGS SOMETHING LIKE THE LIGHTS WHICH GO AND COME IN RUINS IT WAS AT SUCH POINTS THAT THE BARRICADES WERE SITUATED
135-16041-0058 V:0.3829 A:0.3894 D:0.4780 THE REST WAS A LAKE OF OBSCURITY FOGGY HEAVY AND FUNEREAL ABOVE WHICH IN MOTIONLESS AND MELANCHOLY OUTLINES ROSE THE TOWER OF SAINT JACQUES
135-16041-0059 V:0.4328 A:0.4820 D:0.5554 AND WHERE A FEW STREET LANTERNS STILL BURNED THE AERIAL OBSERVER MIGHT HAVE DISTINGUISHED THE METALLIC GLEAM OF SWORDS AND BAYONETS THE DULL RUMBLE OF ARTILLERY AND THE SWARMING OF SILENT BATTALIONS WHOSE RANKS WERE SWELLING FROM MINUTE TO MINUTE
135-16041-0060 V:0.3934 A:0.3411 D:0.4450 AND AS WE HAVE JUST SEEN ANY STREET WHICH ONE MIGHT COME TO OFFERED NOTHING BUT DARKNESS
135-16041-0061 V:0.3606 A:0.4670 D:0.5621 A WILD DARKNESS FULL OF TRAPS FULL OF UNSEEN AND FORMIDABLE SHOCKS INTO WHICH IT WAS ALARMING TO PENETRATE
135-16041-0062 V:0.3375 A:0.3403 D:0.4497 ALL WAS OVER
135-16041-0063 V:0.4164 A:0.5474 D:0.6173 NO MORE LIGHT WAS TO BE HOPED FOR HENCEFORTH EXCEPT THE LIGHTNING OF GUNS NO FURTHER ENCOUNTER EXCEPT THE ABRUPT AND RAPID APPARITION OF DEATH
135-16041-0064 V:0.3812 A:0.5261 D:0.5595 WHERE
135-16041-0065 V:0.4143 A:0.5270 D:0.5632 HOW
135-16041-0066 V:0.3899 A:0.5855 D:0.6023 WHEN
135-16041-0067 V:0.4283 A:0.5474 D:0.6077 NO ONE KNEW BUT IT WAS CERTAIN AND INEVITABLE
135-16041-0068 V:0.4331 A:0.5450 D:0.6214 IN THIS PLACE WHICH HAD BEEN MARKED OUT FOR THE STRUGGLE THE GOVERNMENT AND THE INSURRECTION THE NATIONAL GUARD AND POPULAR SOCIETIES THE BOURGEOIS AND THE UPRISING GROPING THEIR WAY
135-16041-0069 V:0.3009 A:0.4890 D:0.5867 THAT THE MOST TIMID FELT THEMSELVES SEIZED WITH RESOLUTION AND THE MOST DARING WITH TERROR
135-16041-0070 V:0.3767 A:0.5122 D:0.6210 MOREOVER ON BOTH SIDES THE FURY THE RAGE AND THE DETERMINATION WERE EQUAL
135-16041-0071 V:0.3679 A:0.4540 D:0.5544 FOR THE ONE PARTY TO ADVANCE MEANT DEATH AND NO ONE DREAMED OF RETREATING FOR THE OTHER TO REMAIN MEANT DEATH AND NO ONE DREAMED OF FLIGHT
135-16041-0072 V:0.3791 A:0.5349 D:0.6171 IT WAS INDISPENSABLE THAT ALL SHOULD BE ENDED ON THE FOLLOWING DAY THAT TRIUMPH SHOULD REST EITHER HERE OR THERE THAT THE INSURRECTION SHOULD PROVE ITSELF A REVOLUTION OR A SKIRMISH
135-16041-0073 V:0.5734 A:0.5787 D:0.6623 THE GOVERNMENT UNDERSTOOD THIS AS WELL AS THE PARTIES THE MOST INSIGNIFICANT BOURGEOIS FELT IT
135-16041-0074 V:0.4228 A:0.4231 D:0.5215 HERE ONLY ONE SOUND WAS AUDIBLE A SOUND AS HEART RENDING AS THE DEATH RATTLE
135-16041-0075 V:0.4467 A:0.4131 D:0.5402 NATURE SEEMED TO HAVE FALLEN INTO ACCORD WITH WHAT MEN WERE ABOUT TO DO
135-16041-0077 V:0.4786 A:0.4365 D:0.5178 THE STARS HAD DISAPPEARED HEAVY CLOUDS FILLED THE HORIZON WITH THEIR MELANCHOLY FOLDS
135-16041-0078 V:0.4076 A:0.5328 D:0.6054 WHICH HAD ALREADY WITNESSED SO MANY REVOLUTIONARY EVENTS WHILE YOUTH THE SECRET ASSOCIATIONS THE SCHOOLS IN THE NAME OF PRINCIPLES AND THE MIDDLE CLASSES IN THE NAME OF INTERESTS CLASPING AND THROWING EACH OTHER WHILE EACH ONE HASTENED AND INVITED THE LAST AND DECISIVE HOUR OF THE CRISIS FAR AWAY AND QUITE OUTSIDE OF THIS FATAL QUARTER IN THE MOST PROFOUND DEPTHS OF THE UNFATHOMABLE CAVITIES OF THAT WRETCHED OLD PARIS WHICH DISAPPEARS UNDER THE SPLENDOR OF HAPPY AND OPULENT PARIS THE SOMBRE VOICE OF THE PEOPLE COULD BE HEARD GIVING UTTERANCE TO A DULL ROAR
135-16041-0079 V:0.4202 A:0.4043 D:0.4974 A FEARFUL AND SACRED VOICE
135-16042-0000 V:0.4102 A:0.4348 D:0.5160 IT WAS THE REFLECTION OF THE TORCH WHICH WAS BURNING IN THE CORINTHE BARRICADE
135-16042-0001 V:0.4383 A:0.4018 D:0.5044 MARIUS DIRECTED HIS STEPS TOWARDS THAT RED LIGHT
135-16042-0003 V:0.3807 A:0.4523 D:0.5284 AT THE CORNER OF THE LAST HOUSE ON HIS LEFT HE THRUST HIS HEAD FORWARD AND LOOKED INTO THE FRAGMENT OF THE RUE MONDETOUR
135-16042-0004 V:0.4348 A:0.4636 D:0.5212 WHICH CAST A BROAD CURTAIN OF SHADOW IN WHICH HE WAS HIMSELF ENGULFED HE PERCEIVED SOME LIGHT ON THE PAVEMENT A BIT OF THE WINE SHOP AND BEYOND A FLICKERING LAMP WITHIN A SORT OF SHAPELESS WALL AND MEN CROUCHING DOWN WITH GUNS ON THEIR KNEES
135-16042-0005 V:0.4502 A:0.4080 D:0.5075 ALL THIS WAS TEN FATHOMS DISTANT FROM HIM
135-16042-0006 V:0.4215 A:0.3536 D:0.4596 IT WAS THE INTERIOR OF THE BARRICADE
135-16042-0007 V:0.3939 A:0.4279 D:0.5183 THE HOUSES WHICH BORDERED THE LANE ON THE RIGHT CONCEALED THE REST OF THE WINE SHOP THE LARGE BARRICADE AND THE FLAG FROM HIM
135-16042-0008 V:0.3694 A:0.3380 D:0.4471 MARIUS HAD BUT A STEP MORE TO TAKE
135-16042-0009 V:0.4733 A:0.4268 D:0.5234 FOLDED HIS ARMS AND FELL TO THINKING ABOUT HIS FATHER
135-16042-0011 V:0.4117 A:0.6214 D:0.6792 TO OFFER HIS BREAST TO BAYONETS TO SHED HIS BLOOD TO SEEK THE ENEMY TO SEEK DEATH THAT HE WAS ABOUT TO WAGE WAR IN HIS TURN AND DESCEND TO THE FIELD OF BATTLE AND THAT THE FIELD OF BATTLE UPON WHICH HE WAS TO DESCEND WAS THE STREET
135-16042-0012 V:0.4133 A:0.3956 D:0.5097 HE THOUGHT OF HIS FATHERS SWORD WHICH HIS GRANDFATHER HAD SOLD TO A SECOND HAND DEALER AND WHICH HE HAD SO MOURNFULLY REGRETTED
135-16042-0013 V:0.3781 A:0.4789 D:0.5553 HE SAID TO HIMSELF THAT THAT CHASTE AND VALIANT SWORD HAD DONE WELL TO ESCAPE FROM HIM AND TO DEPART IN WRATH INTO THE GLOOM THAT IF IT HAD THUS FLED IT WAS BECAUSE IT WAS INTELLIGENT AND BECAUSE IT HAD FORESEEN THE FUTURE THAT IT HAD HAD A PRESENTIMENT OF THIS REBELLION THE WAR OF THE GUTTERS BLOWS GIVEN AND RECEIVED IN THE REAR IT WAS BECAUSE COMING FROM MARENGO AND FRIEDLAND IT DID NOT WISH TO GO TO THE RUE DE LA CHANVRERIE IT WAS BECAUSE AFTER WHAT IT HAD DONE WITH THE FATHER IT DID NOT WISH TO DO THIS FOR THE SON
135-16042-0014 V:0.3153 A:0.5910 D:0.6379 HE TOLD HIMSELF THAT IF THAT SWORD WERE THERE IF AFTER TAKING POSSESSION OF IT AT HIS FATHERS PILLOW HE HAD DARED TO TAKE IT AND CARRY IT OFF FOR THIS COMBAT OF DARKNESS BETWEEN FRENCHMEN IN THE STREETS IT WOULD ASSUREDLY HAVE SCORCHED HIS HANDS AND BURST OUT AFLAME BEFORE HIS EYES LIKE THE SWORD OF THE ANGEL
135-16042-0016 V:0.1866 A:0.2969 D:0.4184 AND THEN HE FELL TO WEEPING BITTERLY
135-16042-0017 V:0.1441 A:0.3402 D:0.4698 THIS WAS HORRIBLE
135-16042-0018 V:0.3076 A:0.4788 D:0.5151 BUT WHAT WAS HE TO DO
135-16042-0019 V:0.2748 A:0.4771 D:0.5158 LIVE WITHOUT COSETTE HE COULD NOT
135-16042-0020 V:0.2027 A:0.4961 D:0.5648 SINCE SHE WAS GONE HE MUST NEEDS DIE
135-16042-0021 V:0.2368 A:0.4672 D:0.5333 HAD HE NOT GIVEN HER HIS WORD OF HONOR THAT HE WOULD DIE
135-16042-0022 V:0.2926 A:0.4234 D:0.5060 SHE HAD GONE KNOWING THAT THIS MEANT THAT IT PLEASED HER THAT MARIUS SHOULD DIE
135-16042-0023 V:0.4058 A:0.4583 D:0.5179 AND THEN IT WAS CLEAR THAT SHE NO LONGER LOVED HIM
135-16042-0024 V:0.3781 A:0.5130 D:0.5537 SHOULD HE RETREAT AFTER GOING SO FAR
135-16042-0025 V:0.3487 A:0.5519 D:0.6162 SHOULD HE FLEE FROM DANGER AFTER HAVING APPROACHED IT
135-16042-0027 V:0.4146 A:0.5333 D:0.5816 SLIP AWAY ALL IN A TREMBLE SAYING AFTER ALL I HAVE HAD ENOUGH OF IT AS IT IS
135-16042-0028 V:0.2979 A:0.5421 D:0.6110 WHO WERE A MERE HANDFUL AGAINST AN ARMY
135-16042-0032 V:0.3859 A:0.4227 D:0.5131 ALL AT ONCE HE RAISED IT
135-16042-0033 V:0.6287 A:0.4727 D:0.5646 A SORT OF SPLENDID RECTIFICATION HAD JUST BEEN EFFECTED IN HIS MIND
135-16042-0034 V:0.4489 A:0.3784 D:0.4936 THERE IS A WIDENING OF THE SPHERE OF THOUGHT WHICH IS PECULIAR TO THE VICINITY OF THE GRAVE IT MAKES ONE SEE CLEARLY TO BE NEAR DEATH
135-16042-0035 V:0.4782 A:0.4071 D:0.4993 THE VISION OF THE ACTION INTO WHICH HE FELT THAT HE WAS PERHAPS ON THE POINT OF ENTERING APPEARED TO HIM NO MORE AS LAMENTABLE BUT AS SUPERB
135-16042-0036 V:0.2653 A:0.2988 D:0.4142 HE LEFT NONE OF THEM UNANSWERED
135-16042-0037 V:0.2141 A:0.5017 D:0.5914 LET US SEE WHY SHOULD HIS FATHER BE INDIGNANT
135-16042-0038 V:0.2926 A:0.4636 D:0.5586 ARE THERE NOT CASES WHERE INSURRECTION RISES TO THE DIGNITY OF DUTY
135-16042-0039 V:0.2414 A:0.4482 D:0.5252 CIVIL WAR
135-16042-0040 V:0.2927 A:0.5392 D:0.5576 WHAT DOES THAT MEAN
135-16042-0041 V:0.3351 A:0.4543 D:0.5259 IS THERE A FOREIGN WAR
135-16042-0042 V:0.2685 A:0.5280 D:0.5941 IS NOT ALL WAR BETWEEN MEN WAR BETWEEN BROTHERS
135-16042-0043 V:0.3972 A:0.4053 D:0.5164 WAR IS QUALIFIED ONLY BY ITS OBJECT
135-16042-0044 V:0.2578 A:0.5101 D:0.6131 THERE IS NO SUCH THING AS FOREIGN OR CIVIL WAR THERE IS ONLY JUST AND UNJUST WAR
135-16042-0045 V:0.3970 A:0.4840 D:0.5719 UNTIL THAT DAY WHEN THE GRAND HUMAN AGREEMENT IS CONCLUDED WAR THAT AT LEAST WHICH IS THE EFFORT OF THE FUTURE WHICH IS HASTENING ON AGAINST THE PAST WHICH IS LAGGING IN THE REAR MAY BE NECESSARY
135-16042-0046 V:0.2275 A:0.4538 D:0.5709 WHETHER FOREIGN OR CIVIL IS INIQUITOUS IT IS CALLED CRIME
135-16042-0047 V:0.4930 A:0.5071 D:0.5832 OUTSIDE THE PALE OF THAT HOLY THING JUSTICE BY WHAT RIGHT DOES ONE FORM OF MAN DESPISE ANOTHER
135-16042-0048 V:0.3425 A:0.4365 D:0.5313 BY WHAT RIGHT SHOULD THE SWORD OF WASHINGTON
135-16042-0049 V:0.5737 A:0.5047 D:0.5806 THE ONE IS THE DEFENDER THE OTHER THE LIBERATOR
135-16042-0052 V:0.2282 A:0.5129 D:0.5569 WAR OF THE STREETS
135-16042-0053 V:0.2309 A:0.6129 D:0.6040 WHY NOT
135-16042-0054 V:0.5077 A:0.5119 D:0.5790 THAT WAS THE WAR OF AMBIORIX OF ARTEVELDE OF MARNIX OF PELAGIUS
135-16042-0055 V:0.3012 A:0.5443 D:0.6345 BUT AMBIORIX FOUGHT AGAINST ROME ARTEVELDE AGAINST FRANCE
135-16042-0056 V:0.3460 A:0.5330 D:0.6258 AN INVASION VIOLATES THE GEOGRAPHICAL FRONTIER
135-16042-0057 V:0.2435 A:0.5708 D:0.6492 DRIVING OUT THE TYRANT OR DRIVING OUT THE ENGLISH IN BOTH CASES REGAINING POSSESSION OF ONES OWN TERRITORY
135-16042-0059 V:0.4203 A:0.3259 D:0.4310 AFTER DIDEROT DANTON
135-16042-0060 V:0.4058 A:0.4283 D:0.5460 MULTITUDES HAVE A TENDENCY TO ACCEPT THE MASTER
